-- Containment index over a trajectory's constituent ids. THE read model stands on
-- this: compose a point locally from content (a hash, no round-trip), then ask which
-- trajectories CONTAIN it — constituent_ids(trajectory) @> ARRAY[point]. Precedes,
-- follows, contains, part-of and co-occurrence are that same probe read at different
-- offsets, and trajectory_continuations() serves generation from it. Without this it
-- is a sequential scan of every trajectory in the substrate.
--
-- It is also the most expensive index here to maintain: GIN writes one entry per
-- array element and chess trajectories average 137 constituents, so it takes roughly
-- 96% of index-entry writes on this table. That is the price of the capability, not
-- waste. It cannot be narrowed by predicate — the only discriminator that would help
-- (entity type) lives on `entities`, not here.
--
-- fastupdate + the pending list are the lever that IS available. With fastupdate on
-- (the default) inserts land in an unordered pending list, and a backend flushes it
-- into the main structure once it exceeds the limit — in the FOREGROUND of whichever
-- backend crosses the threshold. At the 4 MB default and ~137 entries per row a bulk
-- seed crosses it constantly, so that stall recurs throughout the load; this is the
-- random-write behaviour behind the measured 50 MB/s of WAL producing 2.5 MB/s of net
-- data growth. A larger list batches more entries per merge, and GIN merges are much
-- more efficient in bulk because entries for the same key combine into one posting
-- list update.
--
-- THE TRADE-OFF POINTS THE OTHER WAY ON READS: the pending list is scanned linearly
-- on every search of this index until it is flushed, so an oversized list taxes
-- exactly the probe the index exists to serve. 32 MB is chosen because the write
-- burst is a bulk seed (nothing is querying) while steady state is read-heavy with
-- sparse writes, which keeps the list near-empty when it would otherwise be scanned.
-- A CONSIDERED STARTING POINT, NOT A MEASURED OPTIMUM — re-measure on the next full
-- seed and move it.
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS physicalities_constituents_gin
    ON physicalities USING gin (public.laplace_trajectory_constituent_ids(trajectory))
    WITH (fastupdate = on, gin_pending_list_limit = 32768)
    WHERE type = 1 AND trajectory IS NOT NULL;
